(Kempf)\label{theorem6}
Let $G$ be a reductive group, acting on an affine variety $X$. Let $\chi$ be a character of $G$, and let 
$x\in X$ be a $\chi$-unstable point. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\Lambda^{\chi}(x)$ is not empty;
\item For any $g\in G$, $\Lambda^{\chi}(g\cdot x)=g\Lambda^{\chi}(x) g^{-1}$, and $\mathcal{M}^{\chi}(g\cdot x)=\mathcal{M}^{\chi}(x)$;
\item There is a
  parabolic subgroup $P(\chi,x)$ of $G$ such that for all $\lambda\in \Lambda^{\chi}(x)$, $P(\lambda)= P(\chi,x)$, and such that any two elements of $\Lambda^{\chi}(x)$ are conjugate to each other by an element in $P(\chi,x)$. 
\end{enumerate}

